[2026-02-04T17:43:48.827Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A2U8G1g4tuCkrcsPWALmNK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"fact-check labels reduce engagement 46% reposts social media research study\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Flagging misinformation on social media reduces engagement, study finds | Yale News\",\"url\":\"https://news.yale.edu/2025/09/25/flagging-misinformation-social-media-reduces-engagement-study-finds\"},{\"title\":\"Community notes reduce engagement with and diffusion of false information online - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12478135/\"},{\"title\":\"Community notes reduce engagement with and diffusion of false information online | PNAS\",\"url\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2503413122\"},{\"title\":\"Fact-checking reduces the circulation of misinformation – we should not get rid of it | CEPR\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/fact-checking-reduces-circulation-misinformation-we-should-not-get-rid-it\"},{\"title\":\"Community-based fact-checking reduces the spread of misleading posts on social media\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.08781v1\"},{\"title\":\"Does Fact-Checking Work on Social Media? | Scientific American\",\"url\":\"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/does-fact-checking-work-on-social-media/\"},{\"title\":\"Community Notes Moderate Engagement With and Diffusion of False Information Online\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.13322\"},{\"title\":\"References to unbiased sources increase the helpfulness of community fact-checks | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-09372-6\"},{\"title\":\"HKS Misinformation ReviewJournalistic interventions matter: Understanding how Americans perceive fact-checking labels | HKS Misinformation Review\",\"url\":\"https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/journalistic-interventions-matter-understanding-how-americans-perceive-fact-checking-labels/\"},{\"title\":\"Community Notes Help Reduce the Virality of False Information on X, Study Finds | Newswise\",\"url\":\"https://www.newswise.com/articles/community-notes-help-reduce-the-virality-of-false-information-on-x-study-finds\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found a comprehensive study on this topic. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nResearchers found that after a fact-checking note was attached to a post, it resulted on average in 46.1% fewer reposts, which aligns with your query about the 46% figure.\n\n## The Study Details\n\nThe study was co-authored by researchers at Yale, the University of Washington, and Stanford, and appears in the journal Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences. The researchers analyzed data relating to more than 40,000 X posts for which notes were proposed.\n\n## Broader Engagement Impacts\n\nBeyond reposts, the researchers estimated that after a note was attached to a post, it resulted in 44.1% fewer likes, 21.9% fewer replies, and 13.5% fewer views.\n\n## Important Context\n\nHowever, researchers also found that a lot of the engagement with misleading posts happened before the notes were attached. Over the entire lifespan of the posts, the reductions in engagement were smaller, amounting to 11.6% fewer reposts, 13.3% fewer likes, 6.9% fewer replies, and 5.5% fewer views.\n\nAccording to researcher Johan Ugander, \"Labeling seems to have a significant effect, but time is of the essence. Faster labeling should be a top priority for platforms.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"26b17a16-85df-4d7b-9da4-7c55e026041f","tool_use_result":{"query":"fact-check labels reduce engagement 46% reposts social media research study","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019DjU2ovsBZQnYPZAvCJsif","content":[{"title":"Flagging misinformation on social media reduces engagement, study finds | Yale News","url":"https://news.yale.edu/2025/09/25/flagging-misinformation-social-media-reduces-engagement-study-finds"},{"title":"Community notes reduce engagement with and diffusion of false information online - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12478135/"},{"title":"Community notes reduce engagement with and diffusion of false information online | PNAS","url":"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2503413122"},{"title":"Fact-checking reduces the circulation of misinformation – we should not get rid of it | CEPR","url":"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/fact-checking-reduces-circulation-misinformation-we-should-not-get-rid-it"},{"title":"Community-based fact-checking reduces the spread of misleading posts on social media","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.08781v1"},{"title":"Does Fact-Checking Work on Social Media? | Scientific American","url":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/does-fact-checking-work-on-social-media/"},{"title":"Community Notes Moderate Engagement With and Diffusion of False Information Online","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.13322"},{"title":"References to unbiased sources increase the helpfulness of community fact-checks | Scientific Reports","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-09372-6"},{"title":"HKS Misinformation ReviewJournalistic interventions matter: Understanding how Americans perceive fact-checking labels | HKS Misinformation Review","url":"https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/journalistic-interventions-matter-understanding-how-americans-perceive-fact-checking-labels/"},{"title":"Community Notes Help Reduce the Virality of False Information on X, Study Finds | Newswise","url":"https://www.newswise.com/articles/community-notes-help-reduce-the-virality-of-false-information-on-x-study-finds"}]},"Based on the search results, I found a comprehensive study on this topic. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nResearchers found that after a fact-checking note was attached to a post, it resulted on average in 46.1% fewer reposts, which aligns with your query about the 46% figure.\n\n## The Study Details\n\nThe study was co-authored by researchers at Yale, the University of Washington, and Stanford, and appears in the journal Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences. The researchers analyzed data relating to more than 40,000 X posts for which notes were proposed.\n\n## Broader Engagement Impacts\n\nBeyond reposts, the researchers estimated that after a note was attached to a post, it resulted in 44.1% fewer likes, 21.9% fewer replies, and 13.5% fewer views.\n\n## Important Context\n\nHowever, researchers also found that a lot of the engagement with misleading posts happened before the notes were attached. Over the entire lifespan of the posts, the reductions in engagement were smaller, amounting to 11.6% fewer reposts, 13.3% fewer likes, 6.9% fewer replies, and 5.5% fewer views.\n\nAccording to researcher Johan Ugander, \"Labeling seems to have a significant effect, but time is of the essence. Faster labeling should be a top priority for platforms.\""],"durationSeconds":6.948534999999998}}
[2026-02-04T17:43:49.078Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoUiCq4s1vaxwDVYkUpXVv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Meta fact-checking program 2016-2025 effectiveness misinformation reduction statistics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Meta Ends Fact-Checking, Raising Risks of Disinformation to Democracy - Union of Concerned Scientists\",\"url\":\"https://blog.ucs.org/liza-gordon-rogers/meta-ends-fact-checking-raising-risks-of-disinformation-to-democracy/\"},{\"title\":\"More Speech and Fewer Mistakes - About Meta\",\"url\":\"https://about.fb.com/news/2025/01/meta-more-speech-fewer-mistakes/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Dropped Fact-Checking Because of Politics. But Could Its Alternative Produce Better Results? | TechPolicy.Press\",\"url\":\"https://www.techpolicy.press/meta-dropped-fact-checking-because-of-politics-but-could-its-alternative-produce-better-results/\"},{\"title\":\"Our approach to misinformation | Transparency Center\",\"url\":\"https://transparency.meta.com/features/approach-to-misinformation\"},{\"title\":\"Ask the expert: What Meta’s new fact-checking policies mean for misinformation and hate speech | MSUToday | Michigan State University\",\"url\":\"https://msutoday.msu.edu/news/2025/01/ask-the-expert-what-meta-new-fact-checking-policies-mean-for-misinformation-and-hate-speech\"},{\"title\":\"Fact-checking reduces the circulation of misinformation – we should not get rid of it | CEPR\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/fact-checking-reduces-circulation-misinformation-we-should-not-get-rid-it\"},{\"title\":\"Meta is abandoning fact checking – this doesn’t bode well for the fight against misinformation\",\"url\":\"https://theconversation.com/meta-is-abandoning-fact-checking-this-doesnt-bode-well-for-the-fight-against-misinformation-246878\"},{\"title\":\"QUT - Meta is abandoning fact checking – this doesn’t bode well for the fight against misinformation\",\"url\":\"https://www.qut.edu.au/news/realfocus/meta-is-abandoning-fact-checking-this-doesnt-bode-well-for-the-fight-against-misinformation\"},{\"title\":\"Meta shift from fact-checking to crowdsourcing spotlights competing approaches in fight against misinformation and hate speech\",\"url\":\"https://theconversation.com/meta-shift-from-fact-checking-to-crowdsourcing-spotlights-competing-approaches-in-fight-against-misinformation-and-hate-speech-246854\"},{\"title\":\"Meta ends fact-checking programs, experts discuss motivations, consequences | Virginia Tech News | Virginia Tech\",\"url\":\"https://news.vt.edu/articles/2025/01/meta-fact-checking-program-ends-experts-discuss.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Meta's fact-checking program from 2016-2025 and its effectiveness:\n\n## Program Overview\n\nMeta launched its fact-checking program in December 2016, following concerns about the role that misinformation played in that year's US election. Over the years, it has worked with dozens of partners globally, including Poynter's International Fact-Checking Network (IFCN).\n\n## Program Operations\n\nMeta funded fact-checking partners – such as Reuters Fact Check, Australian Associated Press, Agence France-Presse and PolitiFact – to independently assess the validity of problematic content posted on its platforms. Warning labels were then attached to any content deemed to be inaccurate or misleading.\n\n## Effectiveness Evidence\n\nResearch on the program's effectiveness shows mixed results:\n\n**Positive Findings:** Numerous studies have demonstrated that these kinds of warnings effectively slow the spread of misinformation. Additionally, fact-checking significantly reduces engagement with posts on Facebook rated as false and also decreases users' subsequent activity.\n\n**Limitations:** Fact-checking's effectiveness depends on whether users perceive the role of fact-checkers and the nature of fact-checking organizations as trustworthy. Regardless of the type of content moderation, the practice alone is not effective at reducing belief in misinformation or at limiting its spread.\n\n## Program End\n\nIn January 2025, Meta announced the end of this programme in the US, citing concerns over potential threats to free speech.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"38af541b-77b3-40ec-a32d-ec0c5f74083e","tool_use_result":{"query":"Meta fact-checking program 2016-2025 effectiveness misinformation reduction statistics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Wpde92DnTSHVoqjcp14AQe","content":[{"title":"Meta Ends Fact-Checking, Raising Risks of Disinformation to Democracy - Union of Concerned Scientists","url":"https://blog.ucs.org/liza-gordon-rogers/meta-ends-fact-checking-raising-risks-of-disinformation-to-democracy/"},{"title":"More Speech and Fewer Mistakes - About Meta","url":"https://about.fb.com/news/2025/01/meta-more-speech-fewer-mistakes/"},{"title":"Meta Dropped Fact-Checking Because of Politics. But Could Its Alternative Produce Better Results? | TechPolicy.Press","url":"https://www.techpolicy.press/meta-dropped-fact-checking-because-of-politics-but-could-its-alternative-produce-better-results/"},{"title":"Our approach to misinformation | Transparency Center","url":"https://transparency.meta.com/features/approach-to-misinformation"},{"title":"Ask the expert: What Meta’s new fact-checking policies mean for misinformation and hate speech | MSUToday | Michigan State University","url":"https://msutoday.msu.edu/news/2025/01/ask-the-expert-what-meta-new-fact-checking-policies-mean-for-misinformation-and-hate-speech"},{"title":"Fact-checking reduces the circulation of misinformation – we should not get rid of it | CEPR","url":"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/fact-checking-reduces-circulation-misinformation-we-should-not-get-rid-it"},{"title":"Meta is abandoning fact checking – this doesn’t bode well for the fight against misinformation","url":"https://theconversation.com/meta-is-abandoning-fact-checking-this-doesnt-bode-well-for-the-fight-against-misinformation-246878"},{"title":"QUT - Meta is abandoning fact checking – this doesn’t bode well for the fight against misinformation","url":"https://www.qut.edu.au/news/realfocus/meta-is-abandoning-fact-checking-this-doesnt-bode-well-for-the-fight-against-misinformation"},{"title":"Meta shift from fact-checking to crowdsourcing spotlights competing approaches in fight against misinformation and hate speech","url":"https://theconversation.com/meta-shift-from-fact-checking-to-crowdsourcing-spotlights-competing-approaches-in-fight-against-misinformation-and-hate-speech-246854"},{"title":"Meta ends fact-checking programs, experts discuss motivations, consequences | Virginia Tech News | Virginia Tech","url":"https://news.vt.edu/articles/2025/01/meta-fact-checking-program-ends-experts-discuss.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Meta's fact-checking program from 2016-2025 and its effectiveness:\n\n## Program Overview\n\nMeta launched its fact-checking program in December 2016, following concerns about the role that misinformation played in that year's US election. Over the years, it has worked with dozens of partners globally, including Poynter's International Fact-Checking Network (IFCN).\n\n## Program Operations\n\nMeta funded fact-checking partners – such as Reuters Fact Check, Australian Associated Press, Agence France-Presse and PolitiFact – to independently assess the validity of problematic content posted on its platforms. Warning labels were then attached to any content deemed to be inaccurate or misleading.\n\n## Effectiveness Evidence\n\nResearch on the program's effectiveness shows mixed results:\n\n**Positive Findings:** Numerous studies have demonstrated that these kinds of warnings effectively slow the spread of misinformation. Additionally, fact-checking significantly reduces engagement with posts on Facebook rated as false and also decreases users' subsequent activity.\n\n**Limitations:** Fact-checking's effectiveness depends on whether users perceive the role of fact-checkers and the nature of fact-checking organizations as trustworthy. Regardless of the type of content moderation, the practice alone is not effective at reducing belief in misinformation or at limiting its spread.\n\n## Program End\n\nIn January 2025, Meta announced the end of this programme in the US, citing concerns over potential threats to free speech."],"durationSeconds":7.5723682000000005}}
[2026-02-04T17:43:50.282Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KaqJYA41j2yUFvRkQ1GZ1i","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Meta fact-checking partners funding IFCN organizations 2016-2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Meta drops fact-checking partnerships; global watchdogs scramble - Rest of World\",\"url\":\"https://restofworld.org/2025/meta-drops-fact-checking-partnerships-global-watchdogs-scramble/\"},{\"title\":\"Global Fact-Checking Mentorship Program (closed) - Poynter\",\"url\":\"https://www.poynter.org/ifcn/grants-ifcn/global-fact-checking-mentorship-program/\"},{\"title\":\"From moderation to chaos: Meta’s fact-checking and the battle over truth and free speech - Regina Cazzamatta, 2026\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/14614448251413687\"},{\"title\":\"How Meta's fact-checking program works\",\"url\":\"https://techxplore.com/news/2025-01-meta-fact.html\"},{\"title\":\"Meta built a global fact-checking operation. Will it survive? : NPR\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/01/10/nx-s1-5252738/meta-fact-checking-international\"},{\"title\":\"Community Notes: Crowd Participation and Dependence on Professional Fact-Checking Across Languages\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.19947\"},{\"title\":\"Poynter Institute - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poynter_Institute\"},{\"title\":\"International fact-checking union calls emergency meeting after Zuck's announcement\",\"url\":\"https://www.bizpacreview.com/2025/01/08/international-fact-checking-union-calls-emergency-meeting-after-zucks-announcement-1514610/\"},{\"title\":\"International Fact Checking Network (IFCN) Codes and Principles | RAND\",\"url\":\"https://www.rand.org/research/projects/truth-decay/fighting-disinformation/search/items/international-fact-checking-network-ifcn-codes-and.html\"},{\"title\":\"Meta’s move to end fact-checking reflects turn toward freewheeling internet | Elections | Al Jazeera\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/1/10/metas-decision-to-end-fact-checking-captures-freewheeling-zeitgeist\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. Here are the key findings about Meta's fact-checking partnerships with IFCN organizations from 2016-2025:\n\n## Overview of the Program\n\nSince 2016, Meta has attempted to combat misinformation by partnering with credible fact-checking organizations in 119 countries to label misinformation and link out to explanatory posts from its partners. All of Meta's partners are certified by the International Fact-Checking Network (IFCN), which ensures standardization across the globe.\n\n## Scale and Funding\n\nToday, Meta funds more than 90 fact-checking organizations that work in more than 60 languages around the world. Notably, Meta spent $100m between 2016 and 2022 supporting fact-checking programmes certified by the International Fact-Checking Network, according to the company.\n\nAdditionally, The International Fact-Checking Network at the Poynter Institute partnered with Meta to distribute $450,000 in grant support to support fact-checkers and ecosystem partners to participate in a mentorship program.\n\n## Partnership Termination\n\nAs of January 2025, Meta is ending third-party fact-checking on Facebook, Instagram, and Threads, forcing global organizations to rethink their fight against misinformation.\n\nThe search results reveal the historical relationship between Meta and IFCN-certified fact-checkers spanning nearly a decade, as well as the significant investment Meta made in this ecosystem before announcing the program's discontinuation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"0f7e2470-6c7c-45d5-85f3-9dfbce4a1304","tool_use_result":{"query":"Meta fact-checking partners funding IFCN organizations 2016-2025","results":[{"tool_